It is Thursday evening, half past five.
I am in the sports hall at badminton.
It is summer and it is very hot in the hall.
I take my racket out of my backpack.
Timo, Lena and Max are already waiting at the net.
"Hello everyone, are you ready?" I ask.
"We are already sweating," Timo says and laughs.
Usually we play singles.
But in this weather that is too exhausting.
"Do you prefer playing doubles today?" Lena asks the group.
"Absolutely," I answer.
Then we do not have to run as much.
We position ourselves on the court.
Max and I play against Timo and Lena.
Mostly Max plays very fast.
Today we all hit the ball a bit slower.
Timo plays the ball high in my direction.
I jump and hit the ball perfectly.
"Good shot!" Max calls out.
We win the point and high-five.
